---
import {
  findings,
  interviewers,
  interviewTopics,
  participants,
} from "@/data/milestones/m4-interviews";
---

<section id="m4-interviews" aria-labelledby="m4-interviews-title" class="space-y-10">
  <header>
    <h3 id="m4-interviews-title" class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Interview findings</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      The discussion explored how participants use foreign languages, their experiences with
      learning apps, and their reactions to Native's initial wireframe. The notes record a
      shared discussion with four participants, not four separate interview transcripts.
    </p>
    <dl class="mt-5 grid gap-5 border-y border-gray-200 py-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Interviewers</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-slate-600">{interviewers.join(" and ")}</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Participants</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-slate-600">{participants.join(", ")}</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="m4-findings-title">
    <h4 id="m4-findings-title" class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">What we learned</h4>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      The strongest direction to investigate is helping learners turn familiar words into
      spontaneous conversation. The wireframe feedback also points to clearer navigation,
      explicit learning goals and practice tied to the video content. The changes below are
      proposals for the next iteration, not features already implemented or validated.
    </p>
    <ol class="mt-6 divide-y divide-gray-200 border-y border-gray-200">
      {
        findings.map((finding, index) => (
          <li class="py-6">
            <h5 class="flex gap-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">
              <span class="shrink-0 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
              {finding.title}
            </h5>
            <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
              <div>
                <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Interview evidence</dt>
                <dd class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">{finding.evidence}</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Proposed response</dt>
                <dd class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">{finding.implication}</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </section>

  <aside aria-labelledby="m4-limitations-title" class="border-l-2 border-gray-300 pl-5">
    <h4 id="m4-limitations-title" class="font-semibold text-gray-900">How to interpret these findings</h4>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      This is a small qualitative sample. Agreement in a group discussion is not independent
      confirmation, and preferences about a proposed product do not demonstrate actual usage,
      learning outcomes or willingness to pay. Some prompts suggested answers, including fewer
      lessons and the credibility of real-person videos; these ideas need neutral follow-up
      questions and task-based testing. AI-assisted conversation was Mihai's suggestion in response
      to a question about session preferences, not a feature demonstrated in the interview.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      The written notes do not record a session date, duration, recruitment method or whether
      the discussion took place face to face. Those details need confirmation before assessing
      the milestone's requirement for at least three face-to-face interviews.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="m4-transcript-title">
    <h4 id="m4-transcript-title" class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Interview notes in English</h4>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      Translated and edited from the Romanian notes for clarity, with repetitions reduced and
      related exchanges grouped by topic. Speaker attribution and differing opinions are
      preserved. This is an adapted account, not a word-for-word transcript. Screens are named
      by their function because the original notes use inconsistent screen numbers.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 divide-y divide-gray-200 border-y border-gray-200">
      {
        interviewTopics.map((topic, index) => (
          <details id={`m4-interview-${topic.id}`} class="group py-5">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold leading-relaxed text-gray-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-black">
              {index + 1}. {topic.title}
            </summary>
            <dl class="mt-6 space-y-5">
              {topic.turns.map((turn) => (
                <div class:list={[
                  "grid gap-1 border-l-2 pl-4 sm:grid-cols-[5rem_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:gap-4",
                  interviewers.includes(turn.speaker) ? "border-gray-900" : "border-gray-200",
                ]}>
                  <dt class="text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-gray-900">{turn.speaker}</dt>
                  <dd class="min-w-0 break-words leading-relaxed text-slate-600">{turn.text}</dd>
                </div>
              ))}
            </dl>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</section>